WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.400
Here's what done looks like.

2
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.130
Every Kerberos account
has a reviewed decision,

3
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:07.475
and the root key was checked
without administrator rights.

4
00:00:07.475 --> 00:00:11.331
Retrievers match the reviewed
list, one group per group account,

5
00:00:11.331 --> 00:00:13.950
and every new account
follows the standard.

6
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.866
Every write carried its SailPoint request
and ServiceNow change, the pipeline's

7
00:00:18.866 --> 00:00:21.287
account held only its delegated rights,

8
00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.075
and a person sent the
delegated account steps.

9
00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:26.898
No migration broke the
limits or finished early,

10
00:00:26.898 --> 00:00:30.850
and someone other than the person
who applied each plan approved it.

11
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:32.775
Nothing was deleted by this code.

12
00:00:32.775 --> 00:00:36.947
Every island account has an owner
and an end date inside the deadline,

13
00:00:36.947 --> 00:00:40.387
and every managed account
has a reconciled destination.

14
00:00:40.387 --> 00:00:44.387
Next, Chapter 7 turns to least
privilege for service principals,

15
00:00:44.387 --> 00:00:48.613
and Chapter 12 covers the managed
service account standard itself.

16
00:00:48.613 --> 00:00:49.780
Thanks for watching.
